    "explanation": "FAILS HONESTLY, and this is the most important caveat on the proposal. Bloomberg Law (tier 4 for court-reported facts) and PLANADVISER (tier 3) independently report the $23 million settlement, but NO independent source at tier 4 or above makes an adverse determination about MetLife's conduct that would support a two-band move. The score falls chiefly because MetLife publishes almost nothing about claims handling - an ABSENCE OF DISCLOSURE scored at the low anchor - not because harm was independently established. Recorded as passed:false; this proposal should not be applied without a targeted evidence-gathering pass.",
