  "key_evidence": [
    "SEED-BASELINE RECALIBRATION: MetLife's published 60.9 vector is byte-identical across 22 Fortune-500 companies, verified against fortune-500.json. It was never individually measured.",
    "MetLife publishes almost nothing about the thing it does. It pays insurance claims and releases no data on approvals, denials, complaint volumes or claimant experience. Sixteen of forty subdimensions sit at the low anchor for ABSENCE OF DISCLOSURE - explicitly NOT a finding of harm.",
    "MetLife settled a class action by more than 6,000 retirees over pension calculations for $23 million, one day before trial. The deal permanently increases monthly benefits for married retirees who began receiving them from 2013 - substantive repair, but delivered only at the point of maximum litigation pressure.",
